  "accepted_answers": [
    "Harald III"
  ],
  "explanation": "The original sources (D1S2, D1S6, D1S13) directly identify Harald III as Elisiv of Kyiv's spouse, describing their union as a political alliance between Norway and Kyiv. Harald III is also referred to as Harald Hardrada in the text (D1S6), but this is a name variant referring to the same individual. The claim that Jonathan R. Walker is Elisiv’s spouse (from D2) is fictional and inconsistent with the historical context provided in the first document. Therefore, 'Harald III' is the only valid and supported answer."
}
